tialised**; `pA.count` is stack garbage which then drives `c2Support`'s loop. Rust zero-initialises instead. |\n| U2 | `c2GJK` | `cache->count > 4` | `for (i = 0; i < cache->count; ++i)` writes `verts[i]` past the end of `c2Simplex s` (stack smash) and reads `cache->iA[i]` past `iA[3]`. |\n| U3 | `c2GJK` | `cache->count == 4` | reads `cache->iA[3]` / `cache->iB[3]` out of bounds (they alias `iB[0]` and `div`). The observable outputs happen to be independent of the values read (see `err_gjk_cache_count_four`), which **is** asserted. |\n| U4 | `c2GJK` | `cache->iA[i]` / `cache->iB[i]` outside `[0, proxy.count)` | `pA.verts[iA]` reads an uninitialised (`iA < 8`) or out-of-bounds (`iA >= 8`, `iA < 0`) `c2v`. |\n| U5 | `c2Support` | `verts == NULL`, or `count` larger than the array | unconditional `verts[0]` load / OOB loop. |\n| U6 | any pointer-taking function (`c22`, `c23`, `c2D`, `c2L`, `c2Witness`, `c2GJKSimplexMetric`, `c2BBVerts`, `c2MakeProxy`) | `NULL` pointer argument | the C code dereferences without a guard → `SIGSEGV`. Both builds fault; nothing to compare. |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1194,"cache_read_input_tokens":63160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1194,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6baee55-62af-498d-9859-1b970a6dfa0a","uuid":"b0b11d85-0eb7-4507-9d25-ff7ec7b5313e","timestamp":"2026-08-27T04:08:14.317Z"}
