oad/sign propagation (16 functions)** — the C is built at `-O0`, so each source operation is one SSE instruction, and x86 resolves NaN operands **destination-first**. gcc's destination register isn't always the C expression's left-hand side. 6 of the first 18 tests failed immediately, e.g. `c2Dot` returned `0x7fc01234` where C returned `0xffc01234`. Fixed by modelling the instruction semantics explicitly (`addss/subss/mulss/divss(dst, src)` + `fneg` for C's `xorps`-based unary minus), with each operand order read off `objdump -d`. Notably `c2Add` and `c2CircletoCircle` put the *second* argument in the destination. This also removed a `black_box` hack whose behaviour depended on the optimiser — results are now optimisation-level-independent.\n2. **`c2BBVerts` output/input aliasing** — the C reloads `bb->min`/`bb->max` *after* each store, so an overlapping `out` buffer yields a cascading result (reachable: `c2MakeProxy` passes `p->verts` as `out`). The old snapshot-based code gave the wrong answer and was itself Rust UB.\n3. **`c2Witness` store timing** — the C stores `*a` before evaluating the `*b` expression, so an `a` pointing into `*s` changes `*b`.\n\nFor 2 and 3 I mutation-tested the fixes: reverting each implementation makes its test fail.\n\nAlso hardened: a hostile `c2GJKCache` index used to make the Rust **panic → abort** the process; it now degrades safely.\n\n### Testing\n130 tests, all via `dlopen`/`dlsym` on both `.so`s (never calling Rust directly), compared **bit-exactly**. Includes an exhaustive 12³ distinct-NaN-payload matrix, a 200 000-sample raw-bit-pattern fuzz, and coverage assertions (all 3 `c22` arms, all 7 `c23` arms, both `c2D` arms, both collision outcomes) so a degenerate generator fails rather than silently passing.\n\n`./run_all.sh` runs the full matrix: 3 feature combos × 2 profiles × (1 + 3 seeded soaks) = **24 runs**, plus 168 further ad-hoc seed runs. All pass.\n\n### Two things worth flagging\n- **Four inputs are C undefined behaviour and are deliberately not asserted equal** (`ERRORS.md` U1–U4). I established each boundary experimentally rather than by inspection: `cache->count == 4` makes the C read `iB[3]`, which aliases the *float* `div` reinterpreted as an `int` — with `div == 1.0f` that's vertex index 1065353216 and the test **segfaulted the C**. Separately, a cache index `≥ proxy.count` made the C return stack garbage `(-4.68e-17, 1.53e-41)`. No cache the library itself produces can reach either.\n- **`cargo test` alone does not re-link a `cdylib`**, so it silently tests a stale `.so`. I hit this and added a freshness guard that now refuses to run; use `./run_all.sh` or `cargo build` first.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (md5s verified); only the `build/` directory was added, as instructed.","ttft_ms":3806,"ttft_stream_ms":3660,"time_to_request_ms":38,"type":"result","duration_ms":2737600,"uuid":"b4bb4897-d64c-4e61-8b04-073a1fd34ac6","queued_turn_count":0}
